+ * qemu_crucible_hot_fork_authenticate_immediate_child() - verify fork lineage
+ * @identity: parent identity captured before fork
+ *
+ * Requires the caller to be the immediate child of the exact live process
+ * generation pinned by @identity.  On success the child is armed with
+ * SIGKILL parent-death handling before returning, so the authenticated parent
+ * cannot disappear while the child continues the disposition transaction.
+ *
+ * This function is single-purpose post-fork code.  The caller must terminate
+ * the child after any error and must retain @identity until every operation
+ * requiring the parent anchor is complete.
+ *
+ * Returns zero on success or a negative errno-style status on failure.
+ */
+int qemu_crucible_hot_fork_authenticate_immediate_child(
